## Purpose

Make every durable actionable Tool Shed element report trustworthy local and recursive closure.
The element's versioned immediate-lineage envelope is the recoverable current authority; the
database relationship graph, ancestor paths, blocker rows, and status rollups are guarded,
rebuildable projections. Parent-owned requirements determine whether a child governs closure.

## Desired Outcome

- Every closure-bearing cycle or obligation has a stable identity, versioned subject, explicit
  immediate lineage, and obligation-scoped closure record.
- A parent remains effectively open while any governing requirement or descendant is open,
  missing, stale, invalid, or unreconciled, regardless of the parent's local closure method.
- Status exposes `local_closure`, `evidence_health`, `graph_health`, `effective_closed`, structured
  reasons, counts, nearest blockers, and the exact subject/graph/evaluator revisions.
- Normal reads use transactionally maintained projections; an independent recursive evaluator can
  rebuild and prove the same semantic answer from element envelopes and parent requirements.
- Missing parents become bounded recovery cases, never silently dropped children or invented
  parents. Clean checkpoints and release gates require zero unresolved governing orphans.
- Missing evidence can trigger only a predeclared, versioned proof recipe within current authority;
  blocked, stale, malformed, or failed infrastructure never becomes guessed completion.
- Work2 produces one exact development candidate deployed to the isolated web, Linux, and Windows
  development lanes. Work3 qualifies that frozen candidate. Work5 remains a separate production
  decision.

## Selected Architecture

| Surface | Authority | Derived/operational role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Current lineage | Child's versioned immediate-lineage envelope | Relationship assertions preserve history; indexed edges and paths serve traversal |
| Governing scope | Parent-owned requirement and its disposition | Missing fulfillment remains an explicit blocker even when no child exists |
| Local closure | Revision-bound closed-loop or authorized manual-closure record | Manual closure never closes descendants or bypasses protected gates |
| Effective closure | Recursive invariant over local closure, evidence, graph health, and governing descendants | Incremental rollup is valid only when bound to current revisions and parity-proven |
| Recovery | Exact envelope, requirement, assertion, tombstone, checkpoint, and content history | Recovery stubs locate missing authority but cannot synthesize it |
| Automatic proof | Immutable registered checker plus declarative recipe and active authority envelope | Attempts are leased, idempotent, bounded, redacted, and append-only |
| Operator status | One typed local/hosted projection | Friendly labels never overwrite lifecycle, readiness, reconciliation, or closure authority |

